{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1191348-garous-vs-pentex-the-legal-way","id":1191348,"title":"Garous vs Pentex: The Legal Way","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-03-03T08:19:15-08:00","id":1191348,"title":"Garous vs Pentex: The Legal Way","content":"So..i been thinking..it is possible to beat pentex in their own game? like proving what they do, get them sued or whatever? i know that in the long term it wont work but maybe in the short term it can be a bit disrupting for their operations?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-03T08:46:48-08:00","id":1191356,"title":"","content":"You can beat subsidiaries. Sue them individually for harming people or prosecute for corporate malfeasance... getting a smaller arm of the conglomerate to die is tough, but not impossible. Going after one of the 'big ones' like Endron, even from a totally legal angle, is really dangerous. Whatever reprisals Pentex sends aren't all going to be legal, because the Wyrm doesn't play nice.<br /> <br /> You can't beat Pentex.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-03T09:54:15-08:00","id":1191371,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crowley</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1191348-garous-vs-pentex-the-legal-way#post1191348\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So..i been thinking..it is possible to beat pentex in their own game? like proving what they do, get them sued or whatever? i know that in the long term it wont work but maybe in the short term it can be a bit disrupting for their operations?</div> </div> </div> </div>Realistically a lawsuit probably wouldn't get very far - Pentex would use blackmail on whoever was filing the lawsuit, or pay off the judge, or the jury, or the prosecutors, or whomever. I doubt that they would resort to murder too often, when there are less bloody and equally effective. Even in the World of Darkness if everyone who filed lawsuits against a corporation ended up dead there would eventually be an investigation. Pentex has a lot of clout but it's still not unlimited.<br /> <br /> Still, even in the one-in-a-million chance that a lawsuit goes through and succeeds and the subsidiary in question gets hit with a massive fine, most likely the subsidiary declares simply bankruptcy, sells all of its assets to another a shell-corporation also owned by Pentex, and within a couple of weeks it's back to business as usual. The only real change would be the logo on the sign out front.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-03T09:56:54-08:00","id":1191373,"title":"","content":"As a concept, PENTEX doesn't work if it is possible to beat it in a legal way. If it could be, then the game wouldn't need supernaturally powerful werewolves to defeat them. We could just assume normal humans and kinfolk could use the legal system to do so. Garou would not be needed.<br /> <br /> Legal and political tactics are probably tried and have some limited form of success, but any real defeats would not to be done by Garou. Any legal successes would have to be relatively minor (in terms of what PENTEX really wants done), or irrelevant. For example, court orders and protests finally stop some resource extraction operations done in a sensitive area. It appears to be a big victory, but PENTEX had enough time to free the Bane trapped there while the justice system handled it. So even though on the surface it appears PENTEX was defeated, in reality they accomplished their mission.<br /> <br /> So while I think there is a place where legal measures can be taken, in anything that is really relevant the Garou still need to take direct action against the supernatural component. Of course, legal means can be PART of the strategy necessary to stop them. But if that could work only be itself, I think it undermines what the Garou are there to do. Of course, if you only want there to be background setting, then you can have any number of lawsuits, political lobbying, etc. happening done by whoever. That can make good hooks for PCs to enter the story whether it is a Kinfolk legal firm engaged in a lawsuit, a normal human reporter uncovering a story of business corruption, or a news story alerting the PCs of activity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-03T14:20:27-08:00","id":1191450,"title":"","content":"It'd be like the plot of Batman Begins taken to a far-reaching extreme of scope. You'd have to have every Garou guarding every part of the legal system, scraping together every ally among the Fera they could convince to help by each playing the role of Batman in their own right. Given that this isn't playing to the strengths of every last werebeast in every country that Pentex can claim a holding, it's generally more effective for them to do things the illegal or quasi-legal way.<br /> <br /> (1e actually did have a brief alternate campaign pitch for playing Garou as superheroes, incidentally.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-04T19:46:30-08:00","id":1191814,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1191348-garous-vs-pentex-the-legal-way?p=1191373#post1191373\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As a concept, PENTEX doesn't work if it is possible to beat it in a legal way. If it could be, then the game wouldn't need supernaturally powerful werewolves to defeat them.</div> </div> </div> </div>You know, I'm going to disagree to an extent. The issue in my opinion is not can Pentex or its subsidiaries be beaten in court or public opinion, but rather that any such victories are either pyrrhic, unsatisfying to the Garou, or both. The Exxon Valdez disaster is a good illustration of this in the real world. Exxon was defeated in court -- but it took over a decade, and in the end the corporation was able to out-litigate most of the really vulnerable people who were hurt in the disaster. What was left was an award that they managed to whittle down to almost nothing. In the end, they simply had to admit wrong-doing to get a slap on the wrist. Now, that's not exactly a defeat from their point of view (although the PR disaster it became has haunted them to an extent) since such an admission is cheap. Nonetheless, there were very real consequences for the industry as a whole that were difficult to quantify on a quarterly statement. Exploratory drilling (particularly in coastal areas) have become a bureaucratic nightmare precisely because neither the public nor lawmakers have any trust of the industry in general left due to the way Exxon so flagrantly avoided responsibility for their actions almost three decades ago.<br /> <br /> \u200bThe Garou on the other hand would have little patience for so unsatisfying an outcome. Violent retribution is far more immediate and fulfilling to them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/19/w20supporterheavymetal1.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/546/wpur.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/545/7z8m.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/829/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3506-uniform-two-six","name":"Uniform Two Six","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3506_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"455"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-06T00:40:45-08:00","id":1192168,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crowley</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1191348-garous-vs-pentex-the-legal-way#post1191348\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So..i been thinking..it is possible to beat pentex in their own game? like proving what they do, get them sued or whatever? i know that in the long term it wont work but maybe in the short term it can be a bit disrupting for their operations?</div> </div> </div> </div>That's what Kinfolk are for. I can imagine a troupe based setup where the Garou are engaging in the &quot;fight monsters&quot; end of things while the Kinfolk are doing high end legal thrillers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-06T01:28:15-08:00","id":1192175,"title":"","content":"Probably GW and SL or even COG, know how to stand in the way of pentex legally or using humans and kinfolk. But they will never beat Pentex ths way. <br /> A wyrm tainted megacorporation that controls meds, oil, commerce, with ties almost everywhere, it's probably the most dangerous enemy in the world of darkness, even only few vampires have power inside Pentex, and only one of them is in a powerful position.<br /> <br /> By the way, as the 20th book of the wyrm says, there is no fomori, first team veteran or even black spiral dancer that doesn't trambles hearing the howl of the sons of Gaia.<br /> <br /> In other words: violence works really well. Raids at pentex facilites can lead to an HUGE amount of money to spend, time to waste forming new directors and employers, money to spend to silence the media and corrupt police and thousand of other legal issues. <br /> <br /> By the way, using spirits to fight legally it's really fun. Control or modify emails, alarms, send evidences of corruption to the media and so on.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#800000\">-'' </span>We are the unsullied.<br /> We are the inheritors.<br /> We are the Pure <span style=\"color:#800000\">''-</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3773-helur","name":"Helur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3773_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"352"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-07T04:25:32-08:00","id":1192576,"title":"","content":"Sure theirs a Kinfolk lawyer or two who does nothing but this... its one arm of the war but only one arm.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-08T02:34:32-08:00","id":1193025,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Helur</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1191348-garous-vs-pentex-the-legal-way?p=1192175#post1192175\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Probably GW and SL or even COG, know how to stand in the way of pentex legally or using humans and kinfolk. But they will never beat Pentex ths way.</div> </div> </div> </div>Doesn't mean forcing Pentex to fight on Multiple fronts isn't valuable. Every dollar wasted in court, or bribes is a dollar that can't be spent on killing Garou. That in and of itself make the action valuable.<br /> <br /> ...Now I imagine some Glasswalkers throwing up complicated bidding wars to drive up the price of silver.. because the most it costs the harder it is for it to get used on the warriors of Gaia.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-08T02:39:09-08:00","id":1193026,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1191348-garous-vs-pentex-the-legal-way?p=1193025#post1193025\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Doesn't mean forcing Pentex to fight on Multiple fronts isn't valuable. Every dollar wasted in court, or bribes is a dollar that can't be spent on killing Garou. That in and of itself make the action valuable.<br /> <br /> ...Now I imagine some Glasswalkers throwing up complicated bidding wars to drive up the price of silver.. because the most it costs the harder it is for it to get used on the warriors of Gaia.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I didn't say isn't valuable <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#800000\">-'' </span>We are the unsullied.<br /> We are the inheritors.<br /> We are the Pure <span style=\"color:#800000\">''-</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3773-helur","name":"Helur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3773_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"352"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-08T11:26:20-08:00","id":1193219,"title":"","content":"Very good people. Love the ideas.<br /> <br /> Pentex has so many tactics in subversion its going to be hell and high water to make a big impact on a specific branch. I mean realistic terms make all but the most<br /> red tape savy political and well connected powerhouse of a character pretty much easy pickings for the Crop. of Corruption. Although you can hinder the efforts much easier<br /> than stopping them. There will have to be some true inside understanding of its operations to critically hit subsidiaries in the right spot to make them all but useless to the Corp.<br /> Main and its heads.<br /> ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------oh yeah lets drop some cool manipulated orient sayings in here!<br /> For want of a nail.<br /> The Horse Shoe was lost..<br /> For want of a Horse shoe..<br /> The message was not Delivered..<br /> For want of the Undelivered message..<br /> The order could not be carried out..<br /> For want of the order being carried out..<br /> The Samurai could not protect the Emperor..<br /> For want of the Samurai the Emperor was no more...<br /> <br /> And the war was lost.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23973-silentline","name":"Silentline","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23973_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"24"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-13T00:27:36-07:00","id":1194757,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1191348-garous-vs-pentex-the-legal-way?p=1191373#post1191373\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As a concept, PENTEX doesn't work if it is possible to beat it in a legal way. If it could be, then the game wouldn't need supernaturally powerful werewolves to defeat them. We could just assume normal humans and kinfolk could use the legal system to do so. Garou would not be needed.<br /> <br /> Legal and political tactics are probably tried and have some limited form of success, but any real defeats would not to be done by Garou. Any legal successes would have to be relatively minor (in terms of what PENTEX really wants done), or irrelevant. For example, court orders and protests finally stop some resource extraction operations done in a sensitive area. It appears to be a big victory, but PENTEX had enough time to free the Bane trapped there while the justice system handled it. So even though on the surface it appears PENTEX was defeated, in reality they accomplished their mission.<br /> <br /> So while I think there is a place where legal measures can be taken, in anything that is really relevant the Garou still need to take direct action against the supernatural component. Of course, legal means can be PART of the strategy necessary to stop them. But if that could work only be itself, I think it undermines what the Garou are there to do. Of course, if you only want there to be background setting, then you can have any number of lawsuits, political lobbying, etc. happening done by whoever. That can make good hooks for PCs to enter the story whether it is a Kinfolk legal firm engaged in a lawsuit, a normal human reporter uncovering a story of business corruption, or a news story alerting the PCs of activity.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> still, it would be interesting for a game in whic hte garou nation is divided between those who want to try to sue pentex , and those who believe the only way to beat pentex is by using strenght.<br /> then having those willing to sue to be hunted down and killed by pentex, or threatened. and having the garous trying to protect them, knowing that even if they manage to sue pentex, they wont win but keep it against the ropes for a couple of months.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[]